course: dictionary
lesson: 13745
title: Interception: catching something on its way
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An interception is the act of stopping or catching something while it is on its way from one place to another. The word comes from the verb intercept, which means to catch something in the middle of its journey. «The defender made an interception and the crowd cheered.» The defender caught the ball before it reached the other team's player.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The spy's plan failed after the interception of the secret message.» Secret, spy and failed tell you the message was stopped before it reached the person it was meant for. So an interception can mean catching a message secretly.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The goalkeeper's interception saved the game» still makes sense if you put in "catching the ball on its way". Also check the topic: in maths, intercept is a different use, so look at the subject before you decide.
fact: Interception means the act of stopping or catching something on its way from one place to another.
fact: In sport, an interception is catching or taking the ball when the other team passes it, as in netball, rugby and football.
fact: «The interception of messages» means secretly catching or reading a message meant for someone else.
fact: «Interception» is a noun; the verb is «intercept», to catch something in the middle of its journey.
fact: In maths, do not mix it up: intercept there means the point where a line crosses an axis.
exercise: «The defender made a brilliant interception and ran up the pitch.» What is an interception in sport? | *Catching the ball when the other team passes it | Running very slowly | Kicking the ball out of the stadium | Scoring a goal from the corner
exercise: «The spy's interception of the letter gave the detectives a clue.» What does interception mean here? | Posting a letter to a friend | *Stopping a message on its way and reading it secretly | Losing a letter in the post | Reading a book in a library
exercise: Mia catches a cup before it falls off the table. Which word fits what she did? | Introduction | Injection | *Interception | Inspection
test: «The netball player's interception gave her team the ball.» What does interception mean? | *Catching the ball when the other team passes it | Changing the rules of the game | Watching the game from the stands | Dropping the ball on the floor
test: «Police read the interception of the gang's secret message.» What does interception mean? | Losing a phone | *Secretly catching a message meant for someone else | Writing a message to a friend | Sending a message very quickly
exam: Which sentence uses interception in the sense of catching something on its way? | *The fielder's interception stopped the ball before it reached the boundary. | The rain fell on the roof all day. | The cat sat on the mat all afternoon. | We went to the park after lunch.
